Installation Instructions for ucache
------------------------------------

Requirements
------------
 - Windows x64
 - PHP 7.2, non-thread-safe (NTS) x64 build

Building
--------
build.bat builds bin\Release\php_ucache.dll with MSBuild (Visual Studio 2022)
against the PHP 7.2 NTS x64 devel pack, then runs test-build.php with the PHP
found in PHP_DIR. Adjust MSBUILD, DEVEL_DIR and PHP_DIR at the top of
build.bat first.

  build.bat           build and test
  build.bat install   build, copy php_ucache.dll into %PHP_DIR%\ext, delete
                      the bin folder, and test the installed DLL

Installation
------------
1. Copy php_ucache.dll into the PHP extensions folder (the "ext" folder next
   to php.exe, or the folder set by extension_dir in php.ini).

2. Add this line to php.ini:

     extension=php_ucache.dll

3. Restart the web server, or recycle the IIS application pool that runs PHP.

4. Check that the extension is loaded: "php -m" lists ucache, and phpinfo()
   has a ucache section with the ucache.* settings.

Command line (CLI)
------------------
Under the CLI the cache is only created when ucache.enablecli=1, either in
php.ini or on the command line:

  php -d ucache.enablecli=1 script.php

See README.md for the functions, the ucache.* settings and the ucache.php
statistics page (change its default password before use).
